<title>UK: UK's Hamlet says chief A. Dagul resigns.</title>
<headline>UK's Hamlet says chief A. Dagul resigns.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>British clothing supplier and retailer Hamlet Group Plc said on Monday its managing director Anthony Dagul had resigned with immediate effect.</p>
<p>The company said Alan Brierley was appointed interim chief executive of the group.</p>
<p>The company warned in June its pre-tax profits for the year to June 30 would be lower than market expectations.</p>
<p>Since then the company's share price has dropped from about 70 pence to 22 1/2 on Monday.</p>
